now to northern california and a  devastating development in the fight to  control the state's largest wildfire  this year officials say two people were  found dead in a car after the mckinney  fire tore through a neighborhood near  the oregon border the fire has now  burned through an area larger than the  city of seattle and many more people are  unaccounted for jonathan bigliotti is in  siskiyou county in northern california  jonathan good morning  and good morning to you this fire was  driven by high wind and during the worst  of the fire storm flames jumped from  home to home many people actually chose  not to evacuate ahead of time  and were forced to flee as the fire  barreled down  the race to get people to safety and to  locate the missing is underway in the  fire zone there's so much loss  of the families here teams are searching  through destroyed property to locate  residents who may have died in the  flames the fire exploded so quickly in  this neighborhood it engulfed entire  homes everything that you see here just  destroyed the bodies of two people who  officials say waited too long to  evacuate were discovered in this vehicle  after it was engulfed by the fast-moving  inferno when they did try to escape  their driveway gate apparently wouldn't  open it shows how swiftly these fires  move courtney kreider is a spokesperson  for the siskiyou county sheriff's office  she says nearly two dozen people are  still missing and that number could  increase what we're trying to do today  is get a better reference of people that  are either unaccounted for  or unfortunately fatalities  with thunderstorms moving into the  region the damp conditions are helping  firefighters but the massive fire still  burns out of control the lightning  strikes could be disastrous the one  thing we've learned about thunderstorms  is that we can't predict what's going to  happen  of the thousands of evacuees many are  staying at nearby evacuation centers  including 81-year-old harleen schwander  who lost nearly everything but her life  my house is gone all my furniture all my  clothes shoes coats boots  everything's gone  and we counted dozens of homes that look  just like this you can imagine the  difficult task search and rescue teams  now face as they search for the missing  rain overnight helped stop this fire  from progressing but there is still more  wind and possible chances of lightning  in the forecast  jonathan thank you
 

